1
00:00:01,010 --> 00:00:02,900
Your files are backed up.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,970
But if your computer disappeared tomorrow…

3
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:08,030
could you actually rebuild your project?

4
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:15,050
A project can contain thousands

5
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:16,960
of saved files, and still be

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,680
missing one critical dependency.

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:22,700
Ordinary search can tell you what exists.

8
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:23,960
It cannot always tell you

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,940
whether the pieces agree.

10
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:28,990
This is PHOENIX.

11
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:31,100
An evidence-driven recovery-readiness

12
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:35,340
assistant, designed for UGREEN AI NAS.

13
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,260
Three expert agents discover, extract,

14
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:40,660
verify, and explain what your

15
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:43,460
project's own documents say is required.

16
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:47,190
In this local test, the deployment guide

17
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:50,420
requires a production configuration file.

18
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:52,800
The authorized search cannot confirm it

19
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:55,540
at that exact path, and a stale copy

20
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:58,620
in an old backup folder does not count.

21
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:01,860
PHOENIX identifies the documentary blocker,

22
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:04,750
and cites the source, instead of guessing.

23
00:01:06,290 --> 00:01:07,790
Then it goes further.

24
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:09,560
The Evidence Gain Planner names

25
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,100
one first check for each blocker.

26
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:13,370
Why it matters.

27
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:15,410
What evidence would resolve it.

28
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,420
And what will still remain unknown,

29
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:19,320
even after it passes.

30
00:01:22,150 --> 00:01:24,770
After the operator supplies the file,

31
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:26,990
PHOENIX checks the evidence again.

32
00:01:27,030 --> 00:01:28,500
It does not simply accept a

33
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:30,910
claim that the problem was fixed.

34
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:33,560
The Recovery Delta shows what changed,

35
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,550
and what is now supported.

36
00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:36,1000
But a resolved blocker

37
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,150
is not a restored system.

38
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:42,340
When documents disagree,

39
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:44,580
PHOENIX preserves the conflict.

40
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:46,700
When evidence is incomplete,

41
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:49,300
it refuses to invent certainty.

42
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:51,100
Reliable intelligence must

43
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:53,210
know when not to claim success.

44
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:57,270
In eight predefined local test cases,

45
00:01:57,310 --> 00:01:58,780
PHOENIX matched all eight

46
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:01,320
expected verdicts, compared with six

47
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:03,640
for the retrieval-plus baseline.

48
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:07,410
Real NAS validation is the next milestone.

49
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:11,060
Don't just back up your files.

50
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:13,680
Know what the evidence says you can rebuild.

